        "inouts": [],
        "implementation": "cpp",
        "sourceFile": "SDO_READ4.cpp",
        "documentation": "Reads an object of 1 to 4 bytes from a node by SDO. A rising edge of ENABLE starts the read; BUSY is TRUE until it ends, then CONFIRM (DATA holds the value, little-endian and zero-filled, DATALENGTH the byte count) or ERROR with ERRORTEXT stays until ENABLE goes FALSE. NETWORK counts from 1; DEVICE is the node ID or its name; TIMEOUT T#0s uses the network SDO timeout.\nExample: read(ENABLE := start, DEVICE := IO_Module, INDEX := 16#1018, SUBINDEX := 1); IF read.CONFIRM THEN vendor := read.DATA; END_IF;"
      },
      {
        "name": "SDO_WRITE4",
        "inputs": [
          {
            "name": "NETWORK",
            "type": "USINT"
          },
          {
