        "inouts": [],
        "implementation": "cpp",
        "sourceFile": "SDO_WRITE4.cpp",
        "documentation": "Writes an object of 1 to 4 bytes of a node by SDO: the low DATALENGTH bytes of DATA, little-endian. DATALENGTH 0 takes the size from the node's EDS. A rising edge of ENABLE starts the write; then CONFIRM or ERROR with ERRORTEXT stays until ENABLE goes FALSE. NETWORK counts from 1; DEVICE is the node ID or its name; TIMEOUT T#0s uses the network SDO timeout.\nExample: write(ENABLE := set, DEVICE := IO_Module, INDEX := 16#1017, SUBINDEX := 0, DATA := 1000);"
      },
