        ],
        "inouts": [],
        "implementation": "cpp",
        "sourceFile": "GET_CANOPEN_KERNEL_STATE.cpp",
        "documentation": "Gives the network's bus state, in the same call while ENABLE is TRUE: CANOPEN_KERNEL_NO_ERROR, CANOPEN_KERNEL_ERROR_PASSIVE, CANOPEN_KERNEL_BUS_OFF or CANOPEN_KERNEL_NO_DRIVER (link down or missing). NETWORK counts from 1.\nExample: kernel(ENABLE := TRUE); bus_ok := kernel.STATE = CANOPEN_KERNEL_NO_ERROR;"
      },
      {
        "name": "RECV_EMCY",
        "inputs": [
          {
            "name": "NETWORK",
            "type": "USINT"
          },
          {
            "name": "ENABLE",
            "type": "BOOL"
          }
        ],
        "outputs": [
          {
            "name": "CONFIRM",
            "type": "BOOL"
          },
          {
            "name": "ERROR",
            "type": "USINT"
          },
          {
            "name": "ERRORTEXT",
            "type": "STRING"
          },
          {
            "name": "DEVICE",
            "type": "USINT"
          },
          {
            "name": "EMCY",
            "type": "EMCY_ERROR"
          }
        ],
        "inouts": [],
        "implementation": "cpp",
        "sourceFile": "RECV_EMCY.cpp",
        "documentation": "Returns the network's emergency messages one per call while ENABLE is TRUE, oldest first: CONFIRM is TRUE in a call that returns one, with the sender in DEVICE and the message in EMCY. Messages from before the instance's first call are skipped; each instance has its own position. NETWORK counts from 1.\nExample: emcy(ENABLE := TRUE); IF emcy.CONFIRM THEN last_code := emcy.EMCY.ERRORCODE; END_IF;"
      },
      {
        "name": "RECV_EMCY_DEV",
        "inputs": [
          {
            "name": "NETWORK",
            "type": "USINT"
          },
          {
            "name": "ENABLE",
            "type": "BOOL"
          },
          {
            "name": "DEVICE",
            "type": "USINT"
          }
        ],
        "outputs": [
          {
            "name": "CONFIRM",
            "type": "BOOL"
          },
          {
            "name": "ERROR",
            "type": "USINT"
          },
          {
            "name": "ERRORTEXT",
            "type": "STRING"
          },
          {
            "name": "EMCY",
            "type": "EMCY_ERROR"
          }
        ],
        "inouts": [],
        "implementation": "cpp",
        "sourceFile": "RECV_EMCY_DEV.cpp",
        "documentation": "Returns one node's emergency messages one per call while ENABLE is TRUE, oldest first: CONFIRM is TRUE in a call that returns one, with the message in EMCY. Messages from before the instance's first call are skipped; each instance has its own position. NETWORK counts from 1; DEVICE is the node ID or its name.\nExample: emcy(ENABLE := TRUE, DEVICE := IO_Module); IF emcy.CONFIRM AND emcy.EMCY.ERRORCODE <> 0 THEN alarm := TRUE; END_IF;"
      }
    ],
    "types": [
      {
        "name": "CANOPEN_KERNEL_ERROR",
        "kind": "alias",
        "documentation": "The ERROR of the blocks (USINT): CANOPEN_KERNEL_NO_ERROR, _OTHER_ERROR (the node aborted, see ERRORINFO), _TIMEOUT, _BUS_OFF, _ERROR_PASSIVE, _INTERNAL, _WRONG_PARAMETER, _NODE_ID_UNKNOWN, _NET_ID_UNKNOWN, _REQUEST_ERROR, _NO_DRIVER."
      },
      {
        "name": "DEVICE_STATE",
        "kind": "alias",
        "documentation": "The STATE of GET_STATE (USINT): INIT, RESET_COMM, RESET_APP, PRE_OPERATIONAL, STOPPED, OPERATIONAL, UNKNOWN, NOT_AVAIL."
      },
      {
        "name": "TRANSITION_STATE",
        "kind": "alias",
        "documentation": "The STATE of NMT (USINT): START_REMOTE_NODE, STOP_REMOTE_NODE, ENTER_PRE_OPERATIONAL, RESET_NODE, RESET_COMMUNICATION."
      },
